WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.250
Speaker 1: Well, I woke up this morning and
I said to myself, Sir, we should really do

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.250
a show today.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.540
There's a lot going on.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.799
And so here we are.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:11.720
That's the context in which today's program
is being produced.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.350
One programing note, dozens of people writing
to me breathlessly.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.140
You could tell, even though it was written
text, that people were breathless saying,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.960
David, when is your Lex Freedman appearance
coming out?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.910
I don't know the answer, but I. Lex said it
would be three or four days from when we filmed

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.090
it earlier this week.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.140
So I would guess by the end of this week.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.360
But I don't know and I don't have any control
over it.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.360
But I'm is I'm as eager to take a look at
it as some of the other folks in the audience

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.360
are.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.540
So we'll know about that very, very soon.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.540
All right.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.199
Listen, I've been waiting for this and it
is now happening.

00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:54.969
Republicans, right wingers, MAGA types Steven
Crowder and others are now coming after what

00:00:54.969 --> 00:01:01.610
we call no fault divorce, which essentially
translates to they want to force women to

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:08.869
have to stay married unless they can give
what some consider an acceptable reason for

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:11.820
why they should be allowed to get divorced.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.000
What on earth am I talking about?

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.110
Let's backtrack and let's set it up.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:23.940
I had no plan to talk about right wing content
creator Stephen Crowder's divorce on the podcast.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.390
There's really just no reason to talk about
it.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.390
I don't know.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:32.540
There's nothing particularly newsworthy about
it except when I watched his brief explanation

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.791
of the personal trouble that he's having,
including this very contentious divorce, he

00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:44.360
seemed to sort of bemoan the fact that his
wife can just say, hey, I want a divorce,

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.189
and it's called no fault divorce.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:53.520
You don't have to prove that someone cheated
or whatever to justify the divorce.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.870
You're just allowed to say, I don't want to
be in this marriage anymore.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:03.469
And in the video that Steven Crowder put out
about this, he seemed to be sort of suggesting

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:06.170
that that's a problem, that that's not okay.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.830
His wife maybe should be forced to stay married
to him.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.840
And he's not the only one who feels this way.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.840
Let's take a listen.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.280
This is the video from I guess now.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.590
It's been about a week since this news broke
to the extent that it's news.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:27.610
Speaker 2: I have been living with a proverbial
boot on my neck for going on years now.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.680
Since 2021, I've been living through what
has increasingly been a horrendous divorce.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.790
Now, let me say on the outset, to be clear,
there is no infidelity, any kind of physical

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.690
abuse at all on either side.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.830
And no, this was not my choice.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:49.270
My then wife decided that she didn't want
to be married anymore.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.200
And in the state of Texas, that is completely
permitted.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.810
Speaker 1: It's it's permitted.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:55.810
It's allowed.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:03:00.411
As crazy as it is, you're just allowed to
say, I don't want to be married anymore, and

00:03:00.411 --> 00:03:02.110
I can't control that.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.190
So this is now building into a bigger story.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:10.510
And there's a very interesting Rolling Stone
article, The next front in the Republicans

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.120
War on Women.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.940
No fault divorce.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.060
Steven Crowder is part of a growing right
wing chorus calling for an end to modern divorce

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.180
laws.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.670
And the article explains, and you can check
it out.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.159
Steven Crowder is getting a divorce.

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:25.159
He says it's not his choice.

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:27.569
He says his wife is just allowed to do it.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.799
And the article says Crowder's emphasis on
the state of Texas makes it sound like the

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:33.810
Lone Star State is an outlier.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:39.120
But all 50 states and the District of Columbia
have no fault divorce laws on the books, laws

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.819
that allow either party to walk away from
an unhappy marriage without having to prove

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:48.050
abuse, infidelity or other misconduct.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.650
Republicans are now unsure whether this is
something that they actually want.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:59.890
And the article goes on to say, like the Crusades
against abortion and contraception, making

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:03.860
it more difficult to leave an unhappy marriage
is about control.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.310
Crowder's home state could be the first to
eliminate it if the Texas Republican Party

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.599
gets its way.

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:13.980
Last year, the Republican Party of Texas added
language to its platform, calling to an end

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.959
to no fault divorce.

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:22.590
This is another way to potentially control
women.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.090
That's what this is fundamentally about.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.090
No fault.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:31.740
Divorce is a legal process, which basically
just means you can end a marriage without

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:38.990
having to prove that any spouse is at fault
for the breakdown of the marriage and the

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:44.229
history of no fault divorce in the United
States goes back to the early 20th century.

00:04:44.229 --> 00:04:50.690
But it really wasn't until the 1970s that
no fault divorce had widespread acceptance

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.690
and before you had no fault divorce.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:54.789
I sound like Trump.

00:04:54.789 --> 00:04:55.980
Many people don't know this.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.400
A lot of people have no reason to think about
this.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:06.100
But before there was no fault divorce, divorce
laws in the U.S. were based on fault.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:11.540
And what that meant is in order to be granted
a divorce, in order to be allowed to get a

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:16.669
divorce, one spouse had to prove that the
other spouse was at fault for the failure

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:22.610
of the marriage, and often it was adultery,
cruelty, some kind of abandonment like they've

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:29.210
basically left already anyway, sometimes insanity
or, you know, what we might call mental illness.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.840
And then in the sixties and seventies, states
started to rightfully reconsider that and

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.949
say, hey, you know, maybe people in the same
way that they can choose to get married should

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:40.870
just be allowed to choose to no longer be
married anymore.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.949
And California was the first to pass no fault
divorce in 1969.

00:05:44.949 --> 00:05:48.550
And then by the end of the 1970s, most states
had done the same thing.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:54.520
The really important thing to understand here,
aside from what I believe to be the obvious

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:59.961
logic, that you shouldn't have to make a case
to be allowed to get divorced, you should

00:05:59.961 --> 00:06:02.800
just be able to say, I don't want to be married
anymore.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:10.190
It's worth mentioning that no fault divorce
significantly improve the lives of women as

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:15.940
well as children in many situations by giving
them greater legal protections and more equitable

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.669
outcomes in divorce proceedings.

00:06:17.669 --> 00:06:25.069
Now there is the you'll have the men's rights
activists who love to say men routinely and

00:06:25.069 --> 00:06:32.030
and sort of systematically get screwed over
when it comes to custody in divorce proceedings.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.800
And it's unfair in all these different things.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.600
I consider that to be a different issue that
can be discussed on its merits.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:44.099
But understand that prior to the introduction
of no fault divorce, particularly because

00:06:44.099 --> 00:06:49.699
it was during an era where women were statistically
less likely to work, or if they work, they

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:58.819
were statistically likely to be earning less
money than the husband in a heterosexual marriage.

00:06:58.819 --> 00:07:06.009
They were more likely to be dramatically disadvantaged
and controlled by the lack of no fault divorce.

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:11.780
And so no no fault divorce, as obvious as
it is to many of us and as standard as it

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:18.629
is in so many other Western developed nations,
it actually was a really significant change

00:07:18.629 --> 00:07:28.110
and and liberating to some degree, providing
additional rights to many women as it became

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.820
more common during the 1970s.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:37.280
So it's not a surprise given that Republicans
love policy that allows women to be controlled.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.720
Let's control what women can do with their
bodies.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.650
Let's control medically, etc..

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:47.030
Given all of that, it's not a surprise that
they found yet another issue on which they

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.430
want to go back to the 1950s.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.139
And again, that's quite literally what we're
talking about.

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:52.510
This was the law of the land.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.960
In the 1950s started changing.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.970
69 into the seventies.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:04.620
I had an inkling when I saw the Crowder video,
They're going to go after this no fault divorce.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.229
And now that is in and of itself becoming
a bigger story.

00:08:07.229 --> 00:08:08.350
Horrifying stuff.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.350
But it is the party.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:10.900
It is the movement of going back to the 1950s.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:10.902
All right.

